{
  "$defs": {
    "AeCell": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Actual versus expected for one level of one factor (FR-MODEL-50).\n\n`ci_95` is on the **ratio**, not on the actual: an A/E of 1.19 whose interval excludes\n1.0 is a finding, and one whose interval spans it is noise. Without the interval the\ntwo render identically, which is how a thin cell becomes a rating decision.",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "ae": {
          "title": "Ae",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "ci_95": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "maxItems": 2,
              "minItems": 2,
              "prefixItems": [
                {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                {
                  "type": "number"
                }
              ],
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ci 95"
        },
        "expected": {
          "title": "Expected",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "exposure_years": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "description": "Exact decimal as a string; never a binary float (FR-OVR-7).",
              "pattern": "^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Exposure Years"
        },
        "factor": {
          "title": "Factor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "level": {
          "title": "Level",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor",
        "level",
        "actual",
        "expected",
        "ae"
      ],
      "title": "AeCell",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BacktestSummary": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "What a backtest found, before the platform gives it an identity.\n\nThe `DiagnosticsResult` and `ComparisonSummary` split, for the same reason:\n`pricing-core` computes, and does not allocate ids, know about rows in a database, or\nread a clock (ADR-0001).\n\nThe weighting scheme is inside `partition` and is not restated: it is a function of the\nmodel's spec (FR-MODEL-55), and a backtest scores its own model's spec, so it cannot\ndiffer from the fit-time scheme the reader will compare against.",
      "properties": {
        "dataset_version_ref": {
          "title": "Dataset Version Ref",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "fitted_on_ref": {
          "title": "Fitted On Ref",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "model_ref": {
          "title": "Model Ref",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "partition": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PartitionDiagnostics"
        },
        "period_from": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "format": "date",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Period From"
        },
        "period_to": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "format": "date",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Period To"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "model_ref",
        "dataset_version_ref",
        "fitted_on_ref",
        "partition"
      ],
      "title": "BacktestSummary",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CalibrationBin": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Predicted against observed within a predicted-decile bin (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "bin": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Bin",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "predicted": {
          "title": "Predicted",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "bin",
        "rows",
        "predicted",
        "actual"
      ],
      "title": "CalibrationBin",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "LiftBin": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One predicted-decile bin of a lift/gains curve (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "bin": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Bin",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "exposure_years": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "description": "Exact decimal as a string; never a binary float (FR-OVR-7).",
              "pattern": "^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Exposure Years"
        },
        "predicted": {
          "title": "Predicted",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "bin",
        "rows",
        "predicted",
        "actual"
      ],
      "title": "LiftBin",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PartitionDiagnostics": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Every universal metric, for one partition (FR-MODEL-50).\n\nAt fit time one of these describes train and another describes holdout, and neither is\nmeaningful without the other — which is why a *fit* only ever holds them together\n(`UniversalDiagnostics`).\n\nA backtest holds exactly one (`backtests.BacktestSummary`, FR-MODEL-57), and that is not\nthe same defect: its population was never split, so there is no counterpart to withhold,\nand what it is read against is the model's own fit-time holdout on a different artifact.",
      "properties": {
        "ae_by_factor": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AeCell"
          },
          "title": "Ae By Factor",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "ae_overall": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Ae Overall",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "calibration": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/CalibrationBin"
          },
          "title": "Calibration",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "gini": {
          "title": "Gini",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "gini_normalised": {
          "title": "Gini Normalised",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "lift": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/LiftBin"
          },
          "title": "Lift",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "residual_summary": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ResidualSummary"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "weighting": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Weighting"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "weighting",
        "rows",
        "ae_overall",
        "gini",
        "gini_normalised"
      ],
      "title": "PartitionDiagnostics",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResidualSummary": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Distribution summary of the working residuals (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "maximum": {
          "title": "Maximum",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "mean": {
          "title": "Mean",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "minimum": {
          "title": "Minimum",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "p01": {
          "title": "P01",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "p99": {
          "title": "P99",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "std": {
          "title": "Std",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "mean",
        "std",
        "minimum",
        "maximum",
        "p01",
        "p99"
      ],
      "title": "ResidualSummary",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Weighting": {
      "description": "How a metric was weighted (FR-MODEL-55).\n\n`EXPOSURE` for frequency and burning cost, `CLAIM_COUNT` for severity, `COUNT` where\nthe metric genuinely counts rows. The UI labels an unweighted metric on an\nexposure-weighted problem *as such* — which it can only do if the fit said which.",
      "enum": [
        "exposure",
        "count",
        "claim_count"
      ],
      "title": "Weighting",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "The persisted artifact (`02` §4.12, FR-MODEL-57).\n\nImmutable, and enforced at the privilege layer as well as here (FR-DATA-42): a backtest\nis what a monitoring review and a re-approval argue from, and evidence that can change\nafter the decision is not evidence.\n\nNo slug and no version of its own, for the reason `Diagnostics` and `ModelComparison`\nhave none — it is always reached by id, from the Job that produced it or the record that\ncites it. Unlike `Diagnostics` it is **not** one-per-model: a model backtested against\nfour quarters has four, which is the point.",
  "properties": {
    "computed_at": {
      "format": "date-time",
      "title": "Computed At",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "dataset_version_id": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "title": "Dataset Version Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "id": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "title": "Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "job_id": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "format": "uuid",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Job Id"
    },
    "model_id": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "title": "Model Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "summary": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/BacktestSummary"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "model_id",
    "dataset_version_id",
    "computed_at",
    "summary"
  ],
  "title": "Backtest",
  "type": "object"
}
